## Boundary-data status

These are candidate administrative boundaries. They are not an assertion of
legal sovereignty, maritime jurisdiction, or final operational policy, and they
are not approved production geodetic data. No source or government authority is
represented as endorsing GeoSquare.

The included source and packaged boundary resources are recorded in
`release/boundaries/SOURCES.md`, `release/boundaries/ASEAN_BOUNDARY_METADATA.json`, and the
mirrored `src/geosquare_v2/data/registry/boundaries/` files. Each metadata
record provides the corresponding API endpoint, download URL, boundary ID,
year, source, license, and SHA-256 values. The common metadata API pattern is:

```text
https://www.geoboundaries.org/api/current/gbOpen/<ISO3>/ADM0/
```

